# Local working material. This repo is developed alongside a research workspace
# and a generated code graph, both of which sit in the same folder and are not
# part of the published tool. They are kept out of git rather than out of the
# directory, so the working tree stays usable while the repo stays just the tool.
docs/
evidence/
upstream/
graphify-out/
.graphifyignore

# Markdown is private by default.
#
# Notes, working docs and captured output live in this folder next to the code.
# Listing each one by name meant a new note was tracked until someone remembered
# to add it, which is the wrong way round for files that are not meant to ship.
# This fails closed instead: a new .md is ignored unless it is named below.
*.md

# The un-ignored set: conventional public-facing repo docs. Declared up front,
# even though most do not exist yet, so that creating one later does not silently
# produce an untracked file. Root-anchored, so a note that happens to share one of
# these names deeper in the tree stays ignored.
!/README.md
!/CONTRIBUTING.md
!/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
!/SECURITY.md
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/LICENSE.md
# LICENSE with no extension is not matched by *.md and needs no rule.

# GitHub's own markdown surfaces: issue and PR templates, funding notes. Safe as a
# glob because .github/ is not itself excluded; a negation cannot resurrect a file
# inside an excluded directory, which is why the directory rules above are absolute.
!/.github/**/*.md
